I think having to avoid typos is part of the game. NetHack is about 
staying alert and not making mistakes, and that goes as much for the 
physical buttons you press as for the actions you decide to take. If you 
find yourself accidentally hitting certain keys too often, use #adjust 
to move dangerous objects to safer letters.

There's also a built-in typo saver in the form of an amulet of life 
saving. By level 15 you've probably either found one or gotten the 
chance to wish one up.

